      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "Six foam cubes has a combined volume of $162\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.$ Find the side length of a single cube.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the volume of one foam cube:\n\n$$\n\\frac{162\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}}{6}=27\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of one foam cube.\n\nSince the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV={s}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns=\\sqrt[3]{V}=\\sqrt[3]{27}=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side is $3\\,\\text{in}.$",
